ilt Republican, and his enormous spending advantage is shaping the air war, while a favorable environment for the out-of-power party keeps Bottoms within striking distance in this open-seat race.", "watch": "This week's debates and the start of early voting could jolt a race where a single point separates the candidates.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["Open seat: Brian Kemp (R) is not on the ballot."]}, "overview": "Georgia's governor's race is effectively tied entering the final weeks. Keisha Lance Bottoms and Rick Jackson are competing to succeed term-limited Republican Brian Kemp in a state that has leaned slightly Republican in recent elections. Polls since early September consistently show Jackson ahead by one to three points, a shift from summer surveys that had Bottoms slightly ahead. Nearly every professional rating calls the race a tossup, and prediction markets give Bottoms roughly a 46-47% chance of winning.\n\nThe clearest asymmetry is money: Jackson has raised about $119 million to Bottoms' $5.8 million, and news reports describe a staggering Democratic advertising deficit. That gap is partly offset by an electoral environment that has favored the party out of power. Both candidates are campaigning on affordability agendas, and a series of debates this week could move a race this close.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.6414, "margin": 1.75}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.5561, "margin": 0.5}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.5612, "margin": 0.5}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.5894, "margin": 0.8}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.5413, "margin": 0.8}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.5396, "margin": 0.8}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.5736, "margin": 0.8}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.463, "margin": -0.7}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.5513, "margin": 0.5}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.5602, "margin": 0.5}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.4361, "margin": -1.0}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.4421, "m